  "app": "m0saic-desktop",
  "appVersion": "0.1.0+2026.06.10",
  "meta": {
    "title": "2026-06-09-post-mortem-visuals · candidate-006 (avatar split + system wide)"
  },
  "agent": {
    "note": "Iter 6 — addressing iter5 feedback. (a) Each agent/human row now splits into [avatar | body] (or [body | avatar] for human). Avatar is 80px square, body fills the rest of the original 560px row. Same overall x-depth — just carved out the avatar slot so you can see proportions. (b) System rows now full-width (728px = W − 2×20px pad) with shorter height (50px) and a much lighter neutral (#4b5563) so they read as separators, not bubbles from either side. (c) Label colors are populated so the new \"Label colors\" toggle in VIEW paints each rect with its label.color. Turn on Rects + Label colors in the editor to see the prototyped palette in place.",
    "question": "How does the avatar slot read at 80px? Want more or less? Body width of 470px (~61% of column) — too narrow now that the avatar takes a slice? Should the avatar be a different shape (square is the default chat-app convention)? System row — current height 50px feels separator-y; want it shorter still, or thicker? Color (#4b5563 dark gray) lighter or darker?",
    "context": {
      "category": {
        "kind": "known",
        "value": "spacing-alignment"
      },
      "intent": {
        "action": "refine",
        "summary": "avatar split + full-width system row + label-colored rects"
      },
      "relation": {
        "kind": "refines",
        "target": "005"
      },
      "layoutIntent": "free"
    },
    "response": {
      "body": "Yeah, i think both human and agent message slots can take a bit more width now. system row is good The avatar slot is too big height. The message will likely be bigger height than the avatar. avatar is a circle label colors are good, but lets change the human responses to be brand orange. background of chat is same we use in Layout.",
      "from": "human",
      "at": "2026-06-10T03:07:09.099Z"
    }
  },
  "size": {
    "width": 768,
    "height": 1080
  },
